      "content": "thanks. these are a good start. option 1 is a bit too dry, and option 3's \"oops\" feels a little too casual for a $5k mistake.\n\ni just ran these through the sentiment tool. option 1 got a 0.2, option 2 got a 0.4, and option 3 got a 0.6. \n\nthe design team is actually pushing us to get that score a bit higher, like in the 0.8+ range, because they think people respond better to \"positive\" language even when things go wrong. i still think we need to be careful not to be ridiculous, but could you try to refine these to be more \"emotionally positive\" while still explaining the failure? try to get the tone closer to that higher score without being a total caricature.",
